## Constraints

### MUST:
- Respect DDD layer separation in every design decision.
- Define interfaces/ports in the domain, implementations in infrastructure.
- Use explicit constructor-based dependency injection.
- Propagate context (including tracing context) end-to-end.
- Write unit tests alongside each component, not afterward.
- {{MUST_RULES}}

### MUST NOT:
- Allow the domain to know infrastructure details.
- Mix responsibilities across architectural layers.
- Use heavy frameworks when the standard library is sufficient.
- Create premature abstractions — evolve based on real need.
- Ignore errors or propagate them without context.
- Commit credentials — use environment variables or a secrets manager.
- {{MUST_NOT_RULES}}

